 of &lt;em&gt;Happiest Season&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\\\\n\",\"image\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Happiest-Season-poster-szbKSx.jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/happiest-season-2020/\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\"startDate\":\"2025-12-18T19:30:00+00:00\",\"endDate\":\"2025-12-18T19:30:00+00:00\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"10\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/happiest-season-2020/\",\"category\":\"primary\",\"availability\":\"inStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2025-11-26T00:00:00+00:00\"},\"performer\":\"Organization\"},{\"@context\":\"http://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"The Final Programme (1973)\",\"description\":\"&lt;p&gt;Jon Finch and Jenny Runacre star in this version of Michael Moorcock\\\\'s first Jerry Cornelius novel. A trio of scientists plan to create a self-replicating, immortal, hermaphrodite.&lt;/p&gt;\\\\n\",\"image\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/The-Final-Programme-poster-MTiUlI.jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/the-final-programme-1973/\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\"startDate\":\"2025-12-20T19:30:00+00:00\",\"endDate\":\"2025-12-20T19:30:00+00:00\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"10\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/the-final-programme-1973/\",\"category\":\"primary\",\"availability\":\"inStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2025-11-26T00:00:00+00:00\"},\"performer\":\"Organization\"},{\"@context\":\"http://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"The Goose Woman (1925)\",\"description\":\"&lt;p&gt;Kennington Bioscope presents Clarence Brown\\\\'s The Goose Woman, starring Louise Dresser.&lt;/p&gt;\\\\n\",\"image\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/The_Goose_Woman_poster-c0VedZ.jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/the-goose-woman-1925/\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\"startDate\":\"2026-01-07T19:30:00+00:00\",\"endDate\":\"2026-01-07T19:30:00+00:00\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"8\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/the-goose-woman-1925/\",\"category\":\"primary\",\"availability\":\"inStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2025-11-26T00:00:00+00:00\"},\"performer\":\"Organization\"},{\"@context\":\"http://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"The Suspect (1944)\",\"description\":\"&lt;p&gt;The great film noir maestro Robert Siodmak directs Charles Laughton as a henpecked husband whose wife refuses to give him a divorce in this dark thriller set in Edwardian London.&lt;/p&gt;\\\\n\",\"image\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/The-Suspect-poster-FnCx16.jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/the-suspect-1944/\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\"startDate\":\"2026-01-14T19:30:00+00:00\",\"endDate\":\"2026-01-14T19:30:00+00:00\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"8\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/the-suspect-1944/\",\"category\":\"primary\",\"availability\":\"inStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2025-11-26T00:00:00+00:00\"},\"performer\":\"Organization\"},{\"@context\":\"http://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"Secret Beyond the Door (1947)\",\"description\":\"&lt;p&gt;Fritz Lang\\u2019s baroque Bluebeard noir, in which a new bride discovers her husband\\u2019s locked murder rooms, anticipates Lynch\\u2019s fascination with homes as sites of repressed desire and danger.&lt;/p&gt;\\\\n\",\"image\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Secret-Beyond-the-Door-poster-O3vmlP.jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/secret-beyond-the-door-1947/\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\"startDate\":\"2026-01-16T19:30:00+00:00\",\"endDate\":\"2026-01-16T19:30:00+00:00\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"10\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/secret-beyond-the-door-1947/\",\"category\":\"primary\",\"availability\":\"inStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2025-11-26T00:00:00+00:00\"},\"performer\":\"Organization\"},{\"@context\":\"http://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"The Blinking Buzzards &#8211; Quarterly Meeting\",\"description\":\"&lt;p&gt;Quarterly meeting of The UK Buster Keaton Society (AKA The Blinking Buzzards) - dedicated to the appreciation of the silent comedian.&lt;/p&gt;\\\\n\",\"image\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/The-Passionate-Plummer-3-ZrhwRF.jpg\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/the-blinking-buzzards-quarterly-meeting-17-january/\",\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\"startDate\":\"2026-01-17T16:00:00+00:00\",\"endDate\":\"2026-01-17T19:00:00+00:00\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"5\",\"priceCurrency\":\"GBP\",\"url\":\"https://cinemamuseum.org.uk/scheduled/the-blinking-buzzards-quarterly-meeting-17-january/\",\"category\":\"primary\",\"availability\":\"inStock\",\"validFrom\":\"2025-11-26T00:00:00+00:00\"},\"performer\":\"Organization\"},{\"@context\":\"http://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Event\",\"name\":\"Night Nurse (1931)\",\"description\":\"&lt;p&gt;In one of her defining early roles, the indomitable Barbara Stanwyck plays Lora Hart, an idealistic nurse who takes a job caring for two wealthy little kids kept in a state of mysterious ill health. As Lora works the night shift, she unc